# the cases this column serves: a case name or glob per line, then the reason.
# x86_64-linux with the x86-64-v3 level selected changes codegen by packing the
# vector cells its extensions add rows for (the avx2 per-lane shifts, the sse41
# multiply and extends, the ssse3 range) and by converting f16 with f16c, so
# the column serves the vector group and the f16 cases: every other case would
# repeat x86_64-linux.

vec/*  the vector cells the level's extensions pack; x86_64-linux carries every other group.
float/f16_*  the f16c conversions and the arithmetic they carry through binary32 (#3801).
